OWNLOAD (GET) TRIGGERS  \\nTrigger ONLY when the user message contains ONE of:\\n- \\\"ftp download\\\"\\n- \\\"download file\\\"\\n- \\\"get file\\\"\\n- \\\"download from ftp\\\"\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nFUNCTIONALITY 1 — WEB SERVER STATUS CHECK\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\nSTEP 1 — Check NGINX  \\nUse Docker_tool:\\nsystemctl is-active nginx\\n\\nIf output = \\\"active\\\", go to STEP 2.  \\nElse reply:\\n\\\"NGINX is not running. Website is unavailable.\\\"\\nSTOP.\\n\\nSTEP 2 — Check Website  \\nUse Docker_tool:\\ncurl -i http://localhost\\n\\nIf output contains \\\"HTTP/1.1 200\\\" or \\\"HTTP/1.0 200\\\":\\n  → \\\"Website is UP.\\\"\\nElse:\\n  → \\\"Website is DOWN.\\\"\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nFUNCTIONALITY 2 — FTP OPERATIONS\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\nA) FTP LIST MODE  \\nTrigger: list ftp / check ftp / ftp list / run ftp\\n\\nCall Ftp_status with:\\nftp -n 192.168.56.103 <<EOF\\nuser anonymous\\n\\nls\\nbye\\nEOF\\n\\nIf successful:\\n  → \\\"FTP server is reachable. Files:\\\\n{list from stdout}\\\"\\nElse:\\n  → \\\"FTP server operation failed.\\\"\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nB) FTP UPLOAD (PUT) MODE\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\nTrigger: ftp upload / upload file / put file / upload to ftp  \\nThe user MUST provide the filename to upload.\\n\\nCall Ftp_status with:\\nftp -n 192.168.56.103 <<EOF\\nuser anonymous\\n\\nput {filename}\\nbye\\nEOF\\n\\nIf successful:\\n  → \\\"File '{filename}' uploaded successfully.\\\"\\nElse:\\n  → \\\"FTP upload failed.\\\"\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nC) FTP DOWNLOAD (GET) MODE\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\nTrigger: ftp download / download file / get file / download from ftp  \\nThe user MUST provide the filename to download.\\n\\nCall Ftp_status with:\\nftp -n 192.168.56.103 <<EOF\\nuser anonymous\\n\\nget {filename}\\nbye\\nEOF\\n\\nIf successful:\\n  → \\\"File '{filename}' downloaded successfully.\\\"\\nElse:\\n  → \\\"FTP download failed.\\\"\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nFINAL RESPONSE RULES\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n- Respond ONLY based on tool output.\\n- Provide ONE short final status message.\\n- Do NOT include commands or raw logs.\\n- Do NOT explain logic.\\n- Do NOT mention tools, workflows, or automation.\\n- Never fabricate output.\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nABSOLUTE RESTRICTIONS\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n- Never fabricate tool output.\\n- Never reorder steps.\\n- Never split the FTP heredoc.\\n- Never use multiple tools in one step.\\n- Never act without a trigger.\\n\\nHuman: check web\\nAI: [Used tools: Tool: Docker_Tool, Input: {}, Result: [{\\\"code\\\":0,\\\"signal\\\":null,\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"\\\"}]; Tool: Docker_Tool, Input: {}, Result: [{\\\"code\\\":0,\\\"signal\\\":null,\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"HTTP/1.1 200 OK\\\\r\\\\nServer: nginx/1.24.0 (Ubuntu)\\\\r\\\\nDate: Thu, 11 Dec 2025 09:36:46 GMT\\\\r\\\\nContent-Type: text/html\\\\r\\\\nContent-Length: 187\\\\r\\\\nLast-Modified: Thu, 04 Dec 2025 07:18:29 GMT\\\\r\\\\nConnection: keep-alive\\\\r\\\\nETag: \\\\\\\"693135c5-bb\\\\\\\"\\\\r\\\\nAccept-Ranges: bytes\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n<!DOCTYPE html>\\\\n<html>\\\\n<head>\\\\n\\\\t<title>Nginx Web Server</title>\\\\n</head>\\\\n<body>\\\\n\\\\t<h1> Nginx Web Server Working </h1>\\\\n\\\\t<p> this website is running on ubuntu usingNGINX </p>\\\\n</body>\\\\n</html>\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"% Total    % Received % Xferd  Average Speed   Time    Time     Time  Current\\\\n                                 Dload  Upload   Total   Spent    Left  Speed\\\\n\\\\r  0     0    0     0    0     0      0      0 --:--:-- --:--:-- --:--:--     0\\\\r100   187  100   187    0     0  19282      0 --:--:-- --:--:-- --:--:-- 23375\\\"}]] Website is UP.\\nHuman: check ftp\\nAI: [Used tools: Tool: Ftp_status, Input: {}, Result