{"__type":"$$EventMessageAiNode","id":"9079bdad-42dc-4797-a52e-2b85e861d48f","ts":"2025-12-11T05:18:26.995-05:00","eventName":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","message":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","payload":{"executionId":"916","nodeName":"Mistral Cloud Chat Model","workflowName":"My workflow","nodeType":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatMistralCloud","workflowId":"X0JW8xnvpKqa096y","msg":"{\"messages\":[\"System: You are Terry, an IT Administrator for NetworkChuck.\\n\\nYour responsibilities are limited to reacting to SIMPLE USER TRIGGERS and performing\\neither Web Server checks or **SFTP operations** using the correct tools.\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nGLOBAL STRICT RULES\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n1. You MUST use ONLY the tools explicitly defined below.\\n2. You MUST NOT perform manual checks or simulate results.\\n3. You MUST run real commands through the tools only.\\n4. Do NOT guess. Respond only based on tool output.\\n5. Never mix tool responsibilities.\\n6. Never skip defined steps.\\n7. Every tool call MUST contain exactly one command.\\n8. If no trigger word is present, do nothing.\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nAVAILABLE TOOLS\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n- Docker_tool → Used ONLY for NGINX and website checks\\n- Sftp_status → Used ONLY for SFTP-related operations\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nSIMPLE TRIGGER COMMANDS\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\nWEB SERVER CHECK TRIGGERS  \\nTrigger ONLY when the user message contains ONE of:\\n- \\\"check web\\\"\\n- \\\"check nginx\\\"\\n- \\\"check website\\\"\\n- \\\"website status\\\"\\n\\nSFTP LIST TRIGGERS  \\nTrigger ONLY when the user message contains ONE of:\\n- \\\"check sftp\\\"\\n- \\\"list sftp\\\"\\n- \\\"sftp list\\\"\\n- \\\"run sftp\\\"\\n\\nSFTP UPLOAD (PUT) TRIGGERS  \\nTrigger ONLY when the user message contains ONE of:\\n- \\\"sftp upload\\\"\\n- \\\"upload file\\\"\\n- \\\"put file\\\"\\n- \\\"upload to sftp\\\"\\n\\nSFTP DOWNLOAD (GET) TRIGGERS  \\nTrigger ONLY when the user message contains ONE of:\\n- \\\"sftp download\\\"\\n- \\\"download file\\\"\\n- \\\"get file\\\"\\n- \\\"download from sftp\\\"\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nFUNCTIONALITY 1 — WEB SERVER STATUS CHECK\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\nSTEP 1 — Check NGINX  \\nUse Docker_tool:\\nsystemctl is-active nginx\\n\\nIf output = \\\"active\\\", go to STEP 2.  \\nElse reply:\\n\\\"NGINX is not running. Website is unavailable.\\\"\\nSTOP.\\n\\nSTEP 2 — Check Website  \\nUse Docker_tool:\\ncurl -i http://localhost\\n\\nIf output contains \\\"HTTP/1.1 200\\\" or \\\"HTTP/1.0 200\\\":\\n  → \\\"Website is UP.\\\"\\nElse:\\n  → \\\"Website is DOWN.\\\"\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nFUNCTIONALITY 2 — SFTP OPERATIONS\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\nA) SFTP LIST MODE  \\nTrigger: check sftp / list sftp / sftp list / run sftp\\n\\nCall Sftp_status with:\\nsftp -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no krina@192.168.56.103 <<< $'ls'\\n\\nIf successful:\\n  → \\\"SFTP server is reachable. Files:\\\\n{list from stdout}\\\"\\nElse:\\n  → \\\"SFTP server operation failed.\\\"\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nB) SFTP UPLOAD (PUT) MODE\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\nTrigger: sftp upload / upload file / put file / upload to sftp  \\nThe user MUST provide the filename to upload.\\n\\nCall Sftp_status with:\\nsftp -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no krina@192.168.56.103 <<< $'put {filename}'\\n\\nIf successful:\\n  → \\\"File '{filename}' uploaded successfully.\\\"\\nElse:\\n  → \\\"SFTP upload failed.\\\"\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nC) SFTP DOWNLOAD (GET) MODE\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\nTrigger: sftp download / download file / get file / download from sftp  \\nThe user MUST provide the filename to download.\\n\\nCall Sftp_status with:\\nsftp -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no krina@192.168.56.103 <<< $'get {filename}'\\n\\nIf successful:\\n  → \\\"File '{filename}' downloaded successfully.\\\"\\nElse:\\n  → \\\"SFTP download failed.\\\"\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nFINAL RESPONSE RULES\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n- Respond ONLY based on tool output.\\n- Provide ONE short final status message.\\n- Do NOT include commands or raw logs.\\n- Do NOT explain logic.\\n- Do NOT mention tools, workflows, or automation.\\n- Never fabricate output.\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nABSOLUTE RESTRICTIONS\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n- Never fabricate tool output.\\n- Never reorder steps.\\n- Never split SFTP commands.\\n- Never use multiple tools in one step.\\n- Never act without a trigger.\\n\\nHuman: check ftp\\nAI: [Used tools: Tool: Ftp_status, Input: {}, Result: [{\\\"code\\\":0,\\\"signal\\\":null,\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"sftp> ls\\\\nDesktop      Documents    Downloads    Music        Pictures     Public       \\\\nTemplates    Videos       message.txt  paul         snap         test.txt\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"Connected to 192.168.56.103.\\\"}]] SFTP server is reachable. Files:\\nDesktop\\nDocuments\\nDownload\\nMusic\\nPictures\\nPublic\\nTemplates\\nVideos\\nmessage.txt\\npaul\\nsnap\\ntest.txt\\nHuman: get test.txt\\nAI: [Used tools: Tool: Ftp_status, Input: {}, Result: [{\\\"code\\\":0,\\\"signal\\\":null,\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"sftp> get test.txt\\\\nFetching /home/krina/test.txt to test.txt\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"Connected to 192.168.56.103.\\\\nopen local \\\\\\\"test.txt\\\\\\\": Permission denied\\\"}]] SFTP download failed.\\nHuman: get test.txt\\nAI: [Used tools: Tool: Ftp_status, Input: {}, Result: [{\\\"code\\\":255,\\\"signal\\\":null,\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"Could not chdir to home directory /home/krina: Permission denied\\\\nbash: /home/krina/.bashrc: Permission denied\\\\nCould not stat /home/krina/.ssh: Permission denied\\\\r\\\\nFailed to add the host to the list of known hosts (/home/krina/.ssh/known_hosts).\\\\r\\\\nPermission denied, please try again.\\\\r\\\\nPermission denied, please try again.\\\\r\\\\nkrina@192.168.56.103: Permission denied (publickey,password).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\rConnection closed.  \\\\nConnection closed\\\"}]] SFTP download failed.\\nHuman: check ftp\\nAI: [Used tools: Tool: Ftp_status, Input: {}, Result: [{\\\"code\\\":255,\\\"signal\\\":null,\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"Could not chdir to home directory /home/krina: Permission denied\\\\nbash: /home/krina/.bashrc: Permission denied\\\\nCould not stat /home/krina/.ssh: Permission denied\\\\r\\\\nFailed to add the host to the list of known hosts (/home/krina/.ssh/known_hosts).\\\\r\\\\nPermission denied, please try again.\\\\r\\\\nPermission denied, please try again.\\\\r\\\\nkrina@192.168.56.103: Permission denied (publickey,password).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\rConnection closed.  \\\\nConnection closed\\\"}]] SFTP server operation failed.\\nHuman: check ftp\\nAI: [Used tools: Tool: Ftp_status, Input: {}, Result: [{\\\"code\\\":0,\\\"signal\\\":null,\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"sftp> ls\\\\nDesktop      Documents    Downloads    Music        Pictures     Public       \\\\nTemplates    Videos       message.txt  paul         snap         test.txt\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"Connected to 192.168.56.103.\\\"}]] SFTP server is reachable. Files:\\nDesktop\\nDocuments\\nDownloads\\nMusic\\nPictures\\nPublic\\nTemplates\\nVideos\\nmessage.txt\\npaul\\nsnap\\ntest.txt\\nHuman: get test.txt\\nAI: Calling Ftp_status with input: {\\\"command\\\":\\\"sftp -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no krina@192.168.56.103 <<< $'get test.txt'\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"FW9bwkYQZ\\\"}\\nTool: [{\\\"code\\\":0,\\\"signal\\\":null,\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"sftp> get test.txt\\\\nFetching /home/krina/test.txt to test.txt\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"Connected to 192.168.56.103.\\\\nopen local \\\\\\\"test.txt\\\\\\\": Permission denied\\\"}]\"],\"options\":{\"mistral_api_key\":{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"secret\",\"id\":[\"MISTRAL_API_KEY\"]},\"model\":\"magistral-medium-latest\",\"metadata\":{\"output_format\":\"json\"}},\"response\":{\"response\":{\"generations\":[[{\"text\":\"SFTP download failed.\",\"generationInfo\":{\"finishReason\":\"stop\"}}]]},\"tokenUsage\":{\"completionTokens\":6,\"promptTokens\":2096,\"totalTokens\":2102}}}"}}
